Hi Xavier and Antonio,

I am planing to use the code that you have shared in the link.
Before I do so I have few confusions, wanted to check you people once.
It will be great if you help me.

1) There are several lasthbase project in the github. Should I go ahead with https://github.com/piccolbo/lasthbase?

2) I understand that I have to apply the patch https://github.com/xoolive/hbase-rmr/blob/master/lasthbase.diff in the above project to make it work with latest version of HBase. Please correct if I am wrong. I have installed HBase version 0.94.0, revision r1332822. Will this work?

3) In the code example given by you
keyval(k,v[[1]]$val[[1]]$val)
I suppose that "k" is the "Column Name" (c1) and v[[1]]$val[[1]]$val is the value stored in the column for each row. Am I right?
4) What if I have more than one column.
How do I specify that?
list(hadoop = list(libjars=jars,
                                       D="hbase.mapred.tablecolumns=cf1:c1",
                                       D="hbase.mapred.tablecolumns=cf1:c2",
                                       D="hbase.mapred.inputtable=HBASE_TEST"),
                         local=list()), verbose=TRUE)

For other column families will it be
D="hbase.mapred.tablecolumns=cf1:c1",
D="hbase.mapred.tablecolumns=cf1:c2",
D="hbase.mapred.tablecolumns=cf2:c21",

Looking forward to getting help in this regard.

Thanks and regards,
Souvik.

