Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> smac = mapreduce(
>     '/tmp/data.csv',
>     input.format = make.input.format('csv', sep=','),
>     structured = T,
>     map = function(k, v) keyval(k%%3500, v),
>     reduce = function(k,vv) keyval(k, vv)
> )
>

Actually I am seeing something else. If you read a csv, csv has no notion of a key, so all the data goes into v as a data frame with vectorized = T and structured =T and k is NULL if I remember right. So that k%%3500 is probably returning numeric(0) which means there is only one reducer and one single reduce call, which means the list vv (which gets coerced to a data frame because of the structured option), which means you must be running out of memory as well. My guess is v$some.column.name <http://some.column.name>%%3500 is needed there or similar, You may want to simply skip the reducer and try a map only job, be sure that it does what you think it should and then add the reducer back in.

Antonio

